```mdl
verdict F-1.2: Branches use the fork flag on the block, the block id of the base as the branch id, and the predecessor as the fork point.
  status: done
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo/src/Feed.ts#fork, github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo/src/Feed.ts#readBranch, github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/feed/src/feed-store.ts#FeedStore.appendLocal, github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/feed/src/feed-store.ts#inferBranch]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/feed/src/feed-store.test.ts, github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo/src/Feed.test.ts, github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo-client-e2e/src/feed-branch.test.ts]
  walkthrough:
    - The fork call appends the base with a fork request, and the host writes the fork flag and the fork point as the predecessor. github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo/src/Feed.ts#fork
    - A continuation takes the head of its branch as its predecessor. github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/feed/src/feed-store.ts#FeedStore.appendLocal
    - Every store infers the branch on insert, so a replica infers the same branches. github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/feed/src/feed-store.ts#inferBranch
```

